\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.3}{\ignorespaces Spherical harmonic decomposition of the density field of the dark matter distribution in the subhalo. The power spectrum $P_l$ is normalized to the monopole term $P_0$. The dominance of the monopole term ($l=0$) indicates a high degree of spherical symmetry of the system.}}{3}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sphericity_analysis_density}{{1.3}{3}{Spherical harmonic decomposition of the density field of the dark matter distribution in the subhalo. The power spectrum $P_l$ is normalized to the monopole term $P_0$. The dominance of the monopole term ($l=0$) indicates a high degree of spherical symmetry of the system}{figure.caption.4}{}}
